description:
Azimuth's base CSS (dist/index.css:232-234) includes a global rule:

a:hover {
  color: var(--azimuth-color-primary-hover);
  text-decoration: underline;
}

This is too aggressive — it adds underlines to ALL anchors on hover, including nav links, interaction elements, and components that use background-color for hover feedback. Underlines on nav links look broken.

Fix: Remove text-decoration: underline from the global a:hover rule. Components that need underlined-on-hover links (e.g. Breadcrumbs, text links) should add it themselves.

Many components have a flat list of related props that should be grouped into objects for better ergonomics and API surface reduction.

Examples of candidates:

1. DataTable: virtualized, virtualizedThreshold, virtualizedMaxHeight → virtualization: { enabled, threshold, maxHeight }
2. DataTable: searchable, searchPlaceholder, searchColumns, searchColumnSelector, onSearch → search: { enabled, placeholder, columns, columnSelector, onSearch }
3. DataTable: pageSize, defaultPageSize, pageSizeOptions → pagination: { pageSize, defaultPageSize, pageSizeOptions }
4. Carousel: autoPlay, interval, autoRotate → autoplay: { enabled, interval } (combine overlapping autoPlay/autoRotate)
5. DropdownList: searchable + related → search: { enabled, placeholder }

Goal: reduce prop count per component, make APIs self-documenting via grouping. Each grouped object should be optional (undefined = feature off).

Before implementing any changes, we need a spec covering every component with more than 8 props.
